#: includes/privacy/class-gr-privacy-api.php:590
msgid "Marketing analytics (visits, campaign attribution, conversion tracking) store anonymized IP addresses (IPv4 /24, IPv6 /48) and a visitor identifier, only after marketing consent through the WordPress Consent API. Consent can be withdrawn at any time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-gr-privacy-api.php:591
msgid "Security logs keep complete IP addresses for a short retention period on a legitimate-interest basis (protection against bots and abuse, GDPR Recital 49), masked in the admin display, and can be switched to anonymized storage. A lightweight client probe reports automation conclusions (a bot score and automation flags) under the same basis, with no fingerprint data and no persistent identifiers; it can be switched off in the plugin settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-gr-privacy-api.php:592
msgid "Contact details submitted through the site's forms (name and email) are stored encrypted, together with a lead score and a customer segment derived from consented activity. Emails are shown masked in the admin and appear in plaintext only behind an audited reveal."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-gr-privacy-api.php:593
msgid "Funnel journeys record which steps of a site-owner-defined journey a consented session reached. They carry session and visitor identifiers only, never email or IP, and follow the same 30-day retention as the events they derive from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-gr-privacy-api.php:594
msgid "If the site owner enables cart recovery, the billing email you typed at checkout (with your explicit opt-in at the checkout form, and only with marketing consent) is stored encrypted together with the cart contents, so this site can email you a link to finish an abandoned purchase. Every recovery mail carries an unsubscribe link; unsubscribing is permanent for this site. These records follow the cart-abandonment retention (90 days by default) and are covered by the export and erasure tools below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-gr-privacy-api.php:595
msgid "Data leaves this site only for the outbound services the site owner configured (GA4, Meta), never automatically and never without visitor consent. The WordPress personal data export and erasure tools cover this plugin's marketing tables."
msgstr ""

